e needs) so the generated block does not contradict the surrounding narrative.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.064,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/ticket-model.md:12-17 lists five user-facing types and states 'session_log is a gate/lifecycle-exempt type documented ... not here'","common.schema.json:17 ticket_type enum includes internal 'code_review' and 'identity'; :9 ticket_status includes lifecycle 'archived'/'deleted'","search of docs/ticket-model.md finds no mention of code_review/identity; 'archived' appears only incidentally (line 93)"],"finding":"Fitness-for-purpose tension: the hand-maintained prose in docs/ticket-model.md deliberately documents a curated USER-FACING subset — 5 types (task/story/bug/epic/session_log, with session_log noted as 'documented ... not here') and 5 statuses (open/in_progress/blocked/closed/idea) — and never mentions code_review, identity, archived, or deleted. The AC commits to emitting 'all seven current types and statuses' into a block adjacent to that curated prose. The plan does not say how the generated all-seven block reconciles with the surrounding narrative that intentionally scopes out internal/lifecycle types, risking a doc that contradicts itself.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5c9ba3c869178737","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (bullet 2: 'includes all seven current types and statuses') / docs/ticket-model.md:12-17","norm_id":"ndb968293f178e17c","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The generated block lists code_review/identity/archived/deleted with no explanation while the adjacent prose implies only user-facing types/statuses exist — an agent reading the doc is misled about which types are user-creatable."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_referen